## Summary

Investigated Gayle’s broken event image using production logs and her screenshot. Image searches and import succeeded; the page requested the newly saved photo before the background worker had produced its display image and received 404.

Before: saving a selected photo could reload the page before processing finished, leaving a broken image.
Now: shared photo saves await a completion event on the existing image route before returning; calendar and Team pages retain pending photo IDs but construct display URLs only for ready photos.

Processing stays in the existing background worker. Completion uses an event stream rather than polling or slowing the upload handler. Waiting respects photo permissions and ends on processing failure, deletion, loss of visibility, or client cancellation. No schema or production data changes were needed.

Verified with focused photo, blob, calendar-query and image-search tests, race checks, repository-wide go vet, and a real Chrome upload that displayed the saved event image without failed HTTP responses. The requested merge from main reported already up to date, with no conflicts or additional edits.

